            <ArticleTitle>Faked headaches becoming real.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>998-1002</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/head.12122</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In the gangster movie White Heat, the main character, Cody (played by James Cagney), suffers from 2 headache attacks. Here, I analyze these attacks by using the International Headache Society criteria, but an unequivocal diagnosis is not possible. Nevertheless, the attacks play an important role in the narrative and--as representation of something between &quot;real&quot; (mimesis) and not real--provide a ground for reflection on how to think of headache in general.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2013 American Headache Society.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
